The '''Spira Prime''' is the [[Prime]] variant of the {{Weapon|Spira}} throwing daggers, featuring an increase in [[fire rate]], [[reload speed]], [[status chance]], and [[critical multiplier]] in exchange for reduced damage. It was released alongside {{WF|Saryn Prime}} and {{Weapon|Nikana Prime}}.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Ragdolls and pins the target to the wall on a kill.
**Ragdolled bodies fly in a straight line and can damage other enemies in its path.
*Capable of using the thrown-exclusive mod {{M|Concealed Explosives}}.

{{Advantages|
*Tied with normal {{Weapon|Spira}} for the highest critical chance of all throwing-type secondaries.
*Tied with {{Weapon|Aksomati}}/{{Weapon|Aksomati Prime}} and {{Weapon|Plinx}} for the third highest [[critical multiplier]] of all secondaries, behind {{Weapon|Nukor}} and {{Weapon|Kuva Nukor}}.
*[[Silent]].
*Pinpoint accuracy.
}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Projectiles have travel time and travel in an arc, making it hard to hit at longer ranges and achieve headshots.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Spira}}

==Acquisition==
{{PrimeTable}}
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

===Vaultings===
*On [https://www.warframe.com/news/last-chance-for-saryn-prime December 6th, 2017], it was announced that Spira Prime, alongside {{WF|Saryn Prime}} and {{Weapon|Nikana Prime}}, would enter the [[Prime Vault]] and its relics retired from the drop tables on December 12th, 2017. Any preexisting components or fully-built weapons will remain as is.

==Trivia==
*The Spira Prime was originally released in July 2015 on the Chinese build of Warframe, along with Excalibur Umbra Prime and {{Weapon|Nikana Prime}}.
*The Spira Prime was unintentionally leaked in the [[Codex]] following {{Ver|18.4.7|fix}}.
*The drill tip on the Spira Prime spins, making it the only throwing knife secondary with a non-static animated model.
*"''[[wiktionary:spira#Latin|Spira]]''" is the Latin word for "spiral" or "coil". The weapon is named this way due to its spinning tips.

